.TH AS 1
.SH NAME
as \- assemble AT&T syntax i386 source into an ELF32 object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B as
[
.B --elf
]
[
.B --32
]
[
.B \-gkuvxX
]
[
.B \-O\fIlevel\fP
]
[
.B \-EL
]
[
.BI \-march= CPU[,+EXTENSION...]
]
[
.BI \-mtune= CPU
]
[
.B \-o
.I outfile
]
[
.I infile
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I As
translates 32-bit i386 assembly written in AT&T syntax into an ELF32
relocatable object.  The output byte order is always little-endian, regardless
of the byte order of the host running the assembler.
.PP
The accepted instruction set covers the i386 through i686 integer, system and
x87 instruction families, MMX and AMD 3DNow!, SSE through SSE4.2, AMD SSE4a
and system extensions, Cyrix SMM instructions, and VIA/Centaur PadLock
instructions.  GNU-style sections and symbol attributes, numeric local labels,
and the ELF32/i386 REL relocations used by static and PIC programs are also
supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--elf, --32
Select ELF32/i386 output.  These options are accepted for compatibility; ELF32
is the only output format.
.TP
.B \-o \fIoutfile\fP
Write the object to
.IR outfile .
The default is
.IR a.out .
.TP
.B \-u
Report undefined symbols as errors.
.TP
.B \-x
Discard unreferenced local symbols.
.TP
.B \-X
Discard unreferenced local symbols whose names begin with
.B L
or a period.
.TP
.B \-EL
Select little-endian output.  This is the i386 default.
.TP
.B \-EB
Rejected because ELF32/i386 object files are little-endian.
.TP
.BI \-march= CPU[,+EXTENSION...]
Select the accepted instruction set using GNU
.IR as -compatible
CPU and extension names.  Extensions can be prefixed with
.B no
to disable them.  The special CPU names
.B push
and
.B pop
save and restore the current selection.
.TP
.BI \-mtune= CPU
Validate and record a GNU-compatible scheduling CPU selection.  Instruction
encoding is controlled by
.BR \-march .
.TP
.B \--target-help
List supported CPU and extension names.
.TP
.B \--target-info
Print the configured object format, byte order, CPU selections, and ISA mask.
.SH NOTES
AES/PCLMUL, BMI/BMI2, AVX/AVX2, FMA, XOP, and VEX/EVEX/APX/AVX-512 encodings
are outside this assembler's current classic IA-32 scope and are rejected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR ld (1),
.BR nm (1)
